'''The Coombes''' ({{gbmapping|SU228826}}) is a 15.9 [[hectare]] [[biological Site of Special Scientific Interest]]  at [[Hinton Parva, Wiltshire|Hinton Parva]] in the [[Borough of Swindon]], England, notified in 1989.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Coombs, Hinton Parva SSSI |url=https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/SiteDetail.aspx?SiteCode=S1005603&SiteName=&countyCode=48&responsiblePerson=&SeaArea=&IFCAArea= |access-date=26 July 2023 |website=Natural England}}</ref>

Within a steep-sided dry valley on the edge of the [[Marlborough Downs]], the [[chalk grassland]] is important for its variety of grasses and associated species of butterfly.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Citation for The Coombes SSSI |url=https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/PDFsForWeb/Citation/1005603.pdf |access-date=26 July 2023 |website=Natural England}}</ref> The {{Convert|39|acre|adj=on}} site is owned by the [[National Trust]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Coombes, Hinton Parva {{!}} Wiltshire |url=https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/wiltshire/the-coombes-hinton-parva |access-date=2023-07-26 |website=National Trust |language=en}}</ref>

